    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing \u2014 the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) across the application:\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string property in the owner response schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`), so the generated `OwnerDto` now carries the numeric field.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced `getMembershipTier()` with a transient `getMembershipLevel()` implementing the new rule: start at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 noted as reserved for tenure). MapStruct maps this property straight onto the DTO, as it did for the tier.\n\n**Dead-code cleanup** \u2014 the old tier was the only consumer of the transient `householdSize` (the GOLD-for-3+-household branch, now gone). Since the new level is derived purely from the owner's own fields, I removed the `householdSize` field/accessors from `Owner` and the `applyHouseholdSize` / `countHouseholdMembers` helpers plus their three call sites in `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n\n**On the audit line:** the spec called out \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line).\" I checked \u2014 the create audit line (`AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id=... customerCode=... registrationDate=...\")`) never recorded the tier, and no other code did either, so there was nothing recording the tier left to convert to the level. The only place the tier surfaced was the response field, which is now `membershipLevel`.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreNumericLevel`: email + unique name \u2192 `1 + 1 + 1` = level 3) passes.",
