    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- `getMembershipLevel()` lives in the right unit \u2014 alongside the other derived `@Transient` getters on `Owner` (`getMembershipNumber`, `getLocality`, `getInitials`), and follows the same style (small, self-contained, computed from the owner's own fields). The incremental `level++` accumulation with a `Math.min(..., 3)` cap reads naturally and matches the Javadoc.\n- The removal of the `householdSize` transient field, its accessors, and the `applyHouseholdSize`/`countHouseholdMembers` controller helpers is correct and complete: since the level no longer depends on household size, that plumbing is genuinely orphaned and leaving it would have been dead code. No stray callers remain.\n- `householdId` is correctly retained \u2014 it's a persisted field still used by the household-assignment logic (`deriveHouseholdId` / the join logic at lines 594\u2013621), so it was right not to touch it. Nothing is left dangling.\n- Nothing is duplicated, and no class or method is turning into a catch-all. The controller's response-building path (`toOwnerDto` + `applyBulkSignupWarning`) is simpler now that the pre-response household-size population step is gone.\n- The OpenAPI schema change mirrors the model change coherently (type/format/min/max/example all consistent with the 1\u20133 contract).\n\n(Spec-completeness matters such as whether the create audit line now records the level are correctness concerns outside this review's structural remit.)",
